1
00:00:03,720 --> 00:00:08,660
But what hit us here on Wednesday was the
strongest hailstorm I've ever

2
00:00:08,660 --> 00:00:08,920
witnessed.

3
00:00:10,410 --> 00:00:12,030
It ripped leaves off of plants,

4
00:00:12,950 --> 00:00:14,050
broke some car windows,

5
00:00:14,970 --> 00:00:20,140
roughed up the AC units in the education
center, and it hammered our cars.

6
00:00:20,140 --> 00:00:20,760
I

7
00:00:22,260 --> 00:00:24,740
expected that it might rain,

8
00:00:26,230 --> 00:00:31,360
but if I had known that it was going to
hail like that, I would not have left my

9
00:00:31,360 --> 00:00:33,320
car out there in the parking lot.

10
00:00:33,620 --> 00:00:34,240
I would have moved it,

11
00:00:36,520 --> 00:00:37,280
but I didn't know.

12
00:00:38,181 --> 00:00:44,481
The more we know, the more we can control
outcomes, and that is partially

13
00:00:44,481 --> 00:00:45,361
true.

14
00:00:47,031 --> 00:00:53,311
It is good to have weather satellites that
can warn us, that can forecast

15
00:00:53,311 --> 00:00:58,201
what the weather is going to look like so
that we can live wisely in line of that

16
00:00:58,201 --> 00:01:03,981
fact. Information can help us make wise
decisions, but there is a limit to

17
00:01:04,691 --> 00:01:07,141
the wisdom that we are able to gather.

18
00:01:08,011 --> 00:01:11,271
You can't know enough to control your life.

19
00:01:12,241 --> 00:01:14,101
All this I have tested by wisdom.

20
00:01:15,271 --> 00:01:19,411
I said, I will be wise, but it was far from
me.

21
00:01:21,361 --> 00:01:23,641
That which has been is far off and deep,

22
00:01:24,731 --> 00:01:25,271
very deep.

23
00:01:26,521 --> 00:01:27,241
Who can find it out?

24
00:01:28,093 --> 00:01:28,933
They say,

25
00:01:30,843 --> 00:01:34,883
that climate is what you expect and

26
00:01:35,913 --> 00:01:37,893
weather is what you get.

27
00:01:40,143 --> 00:01:44,603
And Proverbs is sort of what we ought to be
able to expect given the fact that

28
00:01:44,603 --> 00:01:47,223
God has created this world and given us his
wisdom to know how it works.

29
00:01:47,503 --> 00:01:50,903
But sometimes, Ecclesiastes is what we get.

30
00:01:52,843 --> 00:01:56,583
And so often, what we get is confusing.

31
00:01:59,333 --> 00:02:00,293
It doesn't make sense.

32
00:02:01,085 --> 00:02:04,575
We want wisdom because we want to live
well.

33
00:02:06,195 --> 00:02:06,995
But in our sin,

34
00:02:08,035 --> 00:02:13,335
we fall prey to foolishness and we invent
our own rebellious schemes.

35
00:02:14,877 --> 00:02:21,297
We want to make sense of the events in our
lives in this fallen world, and we are

36
00:02:21,297 --> 00:02:23,017
prone to do that apart from God.

37
00:02:23,825 --> 00:02:25,345
But, even

38
00:02:26,405 --> 00:02:32,365
the highest, even the most supreme human
authority, is limited.

39
00:02:34,815 --> 00:02:38,455
Nobody can question or challenge the king,
but he's not omniscient.

40
00:02:39,095 --> 00:02:40,515
That's verse 7.

41
00:02:43,255 --> 00:02:44,915
Furthermore, the king is not omnipotent.

42
00:02:45,135 --> 00:02:45,635
That is verse 8.

43
00:02:48,005 --> 00:02:49,425
No man, not even the king,

44
00:02:50,405 --> 00:02:52,265
has the power to retain the spirit.

45
00:02:53,745 --> 00:02:57,745
The word for spirit can also be translated
as wind.

46
00:02:58,656 --> 00:03:02,376
Jesus, looking toward the cross, said this,
John 10:18,

47
00:03:03,506 --> 00:03:07,386
no one takes it that is my life away from
me.

48
00:03:08,326 --> 00:03:10,366
But I lay it down of my own accord.

49
00:03:11,946 --> 00:03:14,686
I have authority to lay it down.

50
00:03:15,566 --> 00:03:20,286
And I have authority to take it back up
again.

51
00:03:21,626 --> 00:03:24,906
This charge I have received from my Father.

52
00:03:27,906 --> 00:03:32,766
[unclear] friends, Jesus stood out and took
the full brunt of the storm of the

53
00:03:32,766 --> 00:03:36,146
wrath of God in our place for us.

54
00:03:37,346 --> 00:03:39,486
And then three days later rose

55
00:03:40,516 --> 00:03:42,436
back to everlasting life.

56
00:03:43,386 --> 00:03:48,866
The only man with the power over the day of
death used that power to go through

57
00:03:48,866 --> 00:03:52,366
it in order to break death's power over
you.

58
00:03:53,066 --> 00:03:57,426
That is the deep, deep wisdom of the
gospel.

59
00:03:58,430 --> 00:04:01,070
Lay down your schemes and trust God's plan.

60
00:04:01,310 --> 00:04:01,730
Brothers and sisters,

61
00:04:03,370 --> 00:04:09,500
God has not promised to explain every bit
of his mysterious providence

62
00:04:09,500 --> 00:04:11,090
to you.

63
00:04:13,420 --> 00:04:18,200
But he has promised to give you what you do
need to follow him faithfully through

64
00:04:18,200 --> 00:04:18,360
it.

65
00:04:19,290 --> 00:04:22,850
Your inability to understand providence
does not mean, friends, that God has

66
00:04:22,850 --> 00:04:26,210
abandoned you, or that there is no scheme
of things.

67
00:04:26,450 --> 00:04:29,830
It doesn't mean that your suffering is
always evidence of your own personal

68
00:04:29,830 --> 00:04:30,410
folly.

69
00:04:32,100 --> 00:04:37,340
You can live faithfully without solving all
the mysteries of your circumstances.
